# Frontend Development Standards

This project uses:

- Next.js 15
- React 19
- App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4
- shadcn/ui
- Framer Motion
- Zustand
- TanStack Query
- React Hook Form
- Zod

Always follow modern React best practices.

---

# Component Design

Always create components that are:

- Small
- Reusable
- Predictable
- Testable

Avoid giant components.

If a component exceeds approximately 250 lines,
consider extracting smaller components.

---

# Component Structure

Prefer this order:

Imports

↓

Types

↓

Constants

↓

Hooks

↓

Functions

↓

JSX

↓

Export

---

# Component Naming

Good

ReservationCard

MenuItemCard

GalleryGrid

HeroSection

CoffeeBadge

NavigationMenu

Bad

Card1

Menu2

Component

Test

MyComponent

---

# Page Responsibilities

Pages should:

- Fetch data
- Compose sections
- Handle metadata

Pages should NOT:

Contain business logic.

---

# Business Logic

Business logic belongs in:

- Hooks
- Services
- Server Actions (when appropriate)

Never inside JSX.

---

# State Management

Use:

React State

↓

Context

↓

Zustand

Choose the simplest solution.

Never use Zustand for local component state.

---

# Data Fetching

Always use:

TanStack Query

Benefits:

- Cache
- Retry
- Optimistic updates
- Background refetch
- Loading state

Never manually duplicate fetching logic.

---

# Forms

Always use:

React Hook Form

+

Zod

Never manually validate forms.

---

# Styling

Use Tailwind utilities only.

Never write inline styles.

Never use CSS Modules unless explicitly required.

Never hardcode colors.

Use design tokens.

---

# Animation

Use Framer Motion.

Animation should be:

Elegant

Minimal

Fast

Purposeful

Avoid flashy animations.

---

# Accessibility

Every button must:

Have an accessible label.

Every image:

Must include meaningful alt text.

Every form:

Must have associated labels.

Support keyboard navigation.

Respect reduced motion preferences.

---

# Images

Always use:

next/image

Optimize images.

Lazy load below-the-fold images.

Use proper sizes.

---

# Performance

Prefer Server Components whenever possible.

Use Client Components only when needed.

Avoid unnecessary use client directives.

---

# Error Handling

Every async UI must include:

Loading state

Empty state

Error state

Retry action when applicable.

---

# Responsive Design

Design mobile-first.

Support:

Mobile

Tablet

Laptop

Desktop

Ultra-wide screens

Never optimize only for desktop.

---

# SEO

Use:

Metadata API

OpenGraph

Twitter Cards

Canonical URLs

Structured Data

Semantic HTML

Every page should have unique metadata.

---

# Quality Checklist

Before completing any frontend task:

✓ Responsive

✓ Accessible

✓ Type-safe

✓ No console.log

✓ No unused imports

✓ Metadata implemented

✓ Images optimized

✓ Animation consistent

✓ Clean code